    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d73">

                <pb facs="0198" n="82" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg82"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 793.94/218.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Guthrie to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-02-01T11:00:00+09:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 1, 1915—11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Our telegram of January 31, 11 a.m.<anchor n="17" xml:id="d73-f1"/> Can not
                    obtain further details concerning Japan’s demands on China but have statement
                    from authority which can be relied on that they do not affect Yangtze valley.
                    Allegations of Chino-German alliance are believed to have emanated from German
                    sources in Peking.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Guthrie.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
